From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] open-tx-isp: make tisp_event_process wait interruptible

tisp_event_process() waits on tevent_info with
wait_for_completion_timeout(), which sleeps in TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE.
The kthread that calls it in a loop (isp_fw_process) therefore shows up
in "D" state for its entire 200 ms idle timeout on every cycle. A D-state
task counts against the Linux load average even though it burns no CPU,
so a camera sitting idle with the streamer holding /dev/isp open reports
a permanent ~1 unit of phantom load. It also cannot be woken by
kthread_stop(), which makes clean teardown hang (the deinit path already
calls kthread_stop() on this thread).

Switch to wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(). The producer side
(complete(&tevent_info)) wakes interruptible and uninterruptible waiters
identically, so event dispatch is unaffected. The only behavior change is
that the thread sleeps in TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE: it no longer inflates load
average, and kthread_stop() can terminate it cleanly. The existing
-ERESTARTSYS branch then becomes reachable and meaningful (it was dead
code because the uninterruptible variant can never return ERESTARTSYS).

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t31/tx_isp_tuning.c
+++ b/driver/t31/tx_isp_tuning.c
@@ -30824,7 +30824,7 @@
 
     /* OEM: wait_for_completion_timeout(&tevent_info, 0x14)
      * 0x14 = 20 jiffies.  At HZ=100 that is 200 ms. */
-    ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&tevent_info, msecs_to_jiffies(200));
+    ret = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&tevent_info, msecs_to_jiffies(200));
 
     if (ret == -ERESTARTSYS) {
         /* OEM: prints "wake up by signal", returns 0 */
